-- Migration 33: Usage event idempotency key (P2 "Modelos, costo y confianza")
--
-- Each usage_event row written by UsageTrackingCallbackHandler
-- (open_notebook/ai/provision.py) now carries the attempt_id of the
-- specific model-invocation attempt that produced it, so a real retry
-- (its own attempt, its own cost) is traceable and distinguishable from an
-- accidental application-level double-write of the same completed
-- response (which attempt_id would reveal as an improbable duplicate).
--
-- Purely additive: existing rows keep attempt_id = NONE (unknown attempt -
-- written before this migration), nothing else changes.
--
-- Budget settings (daily_budget_usd / monthly_budget_usd) live on the
-- SCHEMALESS open_notebook:content_settings record (see migration 23's
-- comment) and need no DEFINE FIELD here.

DEFINE FIELD IF NOT EXISTS attempt_id ON TABLE usage_event TYPE option<string>;
